Cumbria LRF - Fenella - SITREP 9
Time of report: 16/01/2026 0800

1. SITUATION
Incident status: ACTIVE - response
Wind gusts up to 70 mph on exposed routes.

2. SITES AND ROUTES
- QES Kirkby Lnosdale: reopened
- Riverside Community Centre: rest centre OPEN (run by Cumberland Council)
- Keswick School: closed, all residents rehoused (run by Cumberland Council)
- Pooley Bridge crossing: closed as a precaution
- Cockermouth School: open as rest centre
- West Coast Main Line (Carlisle to Lancaster): services resumed
- Glenridding Village Hall: open as rest centre (run by W&F Council)
- the Northside bridge: closed to all traffic
- Fellside Care Home: residents evacuated
- A591 near Thirlmere: remains closed (flooding)

3. AGENCIES RESPONDING
Cumbria Constabulary, North Cumbria Integrated Care NHS Foundation Trust, Cumbria Fire and Rescue Service, Cumberland Council EP team, WFC

4. NEXT MEETING
SCG at 1000. Dial-in details as previously circulated.

